# skill: loop-pattern
# depends: none
# prohibit: none

## Contract

Provides common loop patterns with built-in interruptibility via `keep_running` flag. All loops check `keep_running` before each iteration to allow graceful shutdown.

## Dependencies

- `keep_running` (external global `int` or `bool`): Controls loop termination. Set to 0/false to stop loops.
- Standard C library: `<unistd.h>` for `sleep()`

## Slots

| Slot | Type | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `LOOP_WHILE(cond)` | macro | Infinite loop that breaks when `cond` is false OR `keep_running` becomes false |
| `periodic_tick(fn, interval)` | `void (*)(void), int` | Calls `fn()` every `interval` seconds until stopped |
| `bounded_for(start, end, fn)` | `int, int, void (*)(int)` | Iterates from `start` to `end`, calling `fn(i)` each iteration |

## Boundaries

- `periodic_tick`: interval must be > 0; negative values cause undefined behavior
- `bounded_for`: if `start > end`, function returns immediately without calling `fn`
- All loops honor `keep_running` check before each iteration (not mid-iteration)

## Examples

```c
// Example 1: Infinite loop with condition
while (keep_running && buffer_has_data()) {
    process_buffer();
}

// Example 2: Periodic task
void report_status(void) { printf("Running\n"); }
periodic_tick(report_status, 5);  // Prints "Running" every 5 seconds

// Example 3: Bounded iteration
void print_num(int n) { printf("%d\n", n); }
bounded_for(1, 10, print_num);  // Prints 1 through 10
```

[code]
```c
// Common loop patterns

// Infinite loop with interrupt check
#define LOOP_WHILE(cond) while(keep_running && (cond))

// Periodic tick — calls fn() every interval seconds
void periodic_tick(void (*fn)(void), int interval) {
    while (keep_running) {
        fn();
        sleep(interval);
    }
}

// For loop with bounds check
void bounded_for(int start, int end, void (*fn)(int)) {
    if (start > end) return;
    for (int i = start; i <= end && keep_running; i++) {
        fn(i);
    }
}
```
